Tranche 2 Deliverable 3: the MoneyGram Access sandbox, how far the client gets
and where exactly it stops.

The criterion names "the MoneyGram Access sandbox" and then names the SDF
Stellar Test Anchor as covering the same flows "during MoneyGram onboarding".
This is what happens when the same client is pointed at MoneyGram directly,
with no onboarding done, so that the onboarding gate is a demonstrated fact
rather than an assertion.

  anchor      extmgxanchor.moneygram.com        (testnet)
  account     GC35EAQJPYWZDPOUMOOLGETVTDMG3KQDKOX4ISGOLXS2RR4JLLLGBFF2
  client      anchor/sep_client.py, unchanged, --home-domain is the only difference

== SEP-1, their toml

  SIGNING_KEY               GCUZ6YLL5RQBTYLTTQLPCM73C5XAIUGK2TIMWQH7HPSGWVS2KJ2F3CHS
  WEB_AUTH_ENDPOINT         https://extmgxanchor.moneygram.com/stellarsepservice/auth
  TRANSFER_SERVER_SEP0024   https://extmgxanchor.moneygram.com/stellarsepservice/sep24
  currency USDC             GBBD47IF6LWK7P7MDEVSCWR7DPUWV3NY3DTQEVFL4NAT4AQH3ZLLFLA5

  That issuer is this deployment's USDC. The SAC of USDC:GBBD47IF is
  CBIELTK6YBZJU5UP2WWQEUCYKLPU6AUNZ2BQ4WWFEIE3USCIHMXQDAMA, which is
  contracts.usdc here. So a MoneyGram sandbox deposit would land as exactly the
  asset the Vault custodies, with no swap in the middle.

== SEP-10, their auth

  WORKS. Challenge fetched, verified against their SIGNING_KEY, signed, and a
  JWT returned:

    sub          GC35EAQJPYWZDPOUMOOLGETVTDMG3KQDKOX4ISGOLXS2RR4JLLLGBFF2
    home_domain  extmgxanchor.moneygram.com
    exp          +24h

  No onboarding was needed for this. Their older host,
  extstellar.moneygram.com, refuses the same call with HTTP 400, which is the
  registration gate on the legacy path; the newer one does not gate SEP-10.

== SEP-24, their limits and their transaction

  /info      deposit  USDC enabled, min 15, max 950
             withdraw USDC enabled, min 15, max 2500

  A 5 USDC deposit is refused for being under their minimum, which is their
  business rule answering correctly. At 20 USDC:

    transaction   c18316d7-9626-4365-a34c-35af9b95ecaa
    type          interactive_customer_info_needed
    url           https://extramps.moneygram.com?transaction_id=...&token=...

== Where it stops

  The interactive URL loads the MoneyGram Ramps widget and fails:

    Something went wrong
    We couldn't load the information needed to continue.
    Error code: RMP-01
    Transaction ID: c18316d7-9626-4365-a34c-35af9b95ecaa

  The widget's own URL carries `wallet_provider=` empty. That is the gate: the
  partner is identified to the widget by a registered wallet provider, and this
  one is not registered, so the widget cannot resolve the configuration it needs
  and stops before collecting anything.

== What this means for the deliverable

  Everything the integration owns works against MoneyGram itself: their toml,
  their SEP-10, their SEP-24, their limits, their transaction. What does not
  work is the part that is not code, which is being a registered MoneyGram
  partner, and it fails with their own error code at their own widget.

  That is the onboarding the award refers to when it names the SDF Stellar Test
  Anchor as covering these flows during it. The Test Anchor round trip is in
  docs/evidence/anchor-roundtrip-2026-10-30.log and is closed end to end.
